# Bump aredn-traceroute revision on every change

Whenever you change anything under `contrib/aredn-traceroute/` that affects the built package or its documented version (source, CGI, library, `build.sh`, install docs that embed the APK name, etc.), **increment the package version in the same change set**.

## What to bump

1. In `contrib/aredn-traceroute/build.sh`, increment the patch segment of `-v` (e.g. `0.1.13` → `0.1.14`).
2. Leave `-r r0` unless the user explicitly asks to bump only the APK release field.
3. Update every APK filename / version string in `contrib/aredn-traceroute/README.md` (and any other docs touched in that change) to match the new `-v` value.

## When

- Do this for **every** substantive package edit in the same turn as the edit — do not wait to be asked.
- Skip only for changes that cannot affect a build or published version (e.g. this Cursor rule alone, `.gitignore` for local helpers, comments outside the package).
- If several edits land in one session before a build/commit, bump **once** per logical change set (one new version number), not once per file touch.
- Do not reuse a version that was already built/installed/pushed for a different content change.

## After bumping (when testing/deploying)

Build and install with the new version so the node is not left on a stale APK with the same name.
